\f0\b\fs52 \cf2 PD Model Project \'97 Brief\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs36 \cf3 Brief overview of project scope, objective and a high level overview of the process.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs40 \cf2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs44 \cf2 1. Objective\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs40 \cf2 This project builds and validates a PD / LGD / EAD credit risk model for US small and medium enterprise (SME) loans, estimating a lender's expected loss for a prospective SBA 7(a)-style loan at the point of origination:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 EL = PD \'d7 LGD \'d7 EAD\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0 \cf2 It produces two deliverables: a reproducible Python modeling pipeline, and a whitepaper presenting the methodology and findings.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs44 \cf2 2. Scope & Data\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs40 \cf2 \'95 Source: SBA 7(a) FOIA loan-level data (
\f2 data.sba.gov
\f1 ), sourced directly from the primary agency \'97 not a third-party aggregator.\
\'95 504 program excluded \'97 structurally different (asset-secured, bank + CDC co-lending), not representative of general SME credit risk.\
\'95 Year range: FY2010\'96Present.\
\'95 Full source links at the end of this document.\
\'95 Dataset 2000-2009 held out for backtesting.\
\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs44 \cf2 3. Methodology \'97 high level\

\fs40 Data preparation\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0 \cf2 Structural validation (row counts, duplicates, column integrity), categorical normalization, NAICS grouped to sector level, business age bucketed, and a fixed performance-window target definition built specifically to remove vintage/seasoning bias from a naive resolved-basis default rate.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 \
Feature selection\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0 \cf2 Determined empirically per model, not fixed in advance \'97 IV/WOE screening for PD, variance-explained checks for LGD/EAD. Each model's final feature list is model-specific.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 \
PD model\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0 \cf2 Logistic regression (primary), using custom-built, auditable WOE binning \'97 chosen over a library such as optbinning for full transparency and control over the exact bin-merge rule, at comparable accuracy. XGBoost run as a comparison model.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 \
LGD model\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0 \cf2 XGBoost (primary/final), with a simpler segment-average kept alongside it as an interpretable comparison point.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 \
EAD model\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0 \cf2 GrossApproval directly for term loans (confirmed accurate); a dedicated XGBoost model for revolving lines of credit, where the approved amount alone understates real exposure.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf2 Full modeling decisions, reasoning, and results: MODELING_NOTES.md.
\f1 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs44 \cf2 4. Validation approach\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs40 \cf2 \'95 PD: time-based train/test split, discrimination and ranking metrics appropriate for a rare-event target (AUC, KS, Gini), calibration, walk-forward cross-validation, multicollinearity check.\
\'95 LGD / EAD: R\'b2/MAE compared across model types on a held-out time-based test set, feature-importance checks, and a consistency check reconstructing historical losses from EAD \'d7 LGD together.\
\'95 Class imbalance (~3\'964% default rate) addressed by relying on rarity-robust metrics rather than resampling the data \'97 resampling risks distorting the time-based, cycle-sensitivity design this project is built around.\
\'95 Extended PD validation, both done: PSI (Population Stability Index) confirmed a major population shift between the training era and the held-out FY2000\'962009 recession window; a direct backtest of the frozen PD model against that same window confirmed the model still discriminates well on data it never trained on, while quantifying where its calibration breaks down.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf2 Full validation results, and the technical reasoning behind each metric choice: MODELING_NOTES.md.
\f1 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs44 \cf2 5. Output\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs40 \cf2 \'95 Python implementation: modular pipeline, EDA through modeling, no notebook-only logic.\
\'95 Whitepaper structure: pain-point framing
\f3\b \cf2 \uc0\u8594 
\f1\b0 \cf2  methodology
\f3\b \cf2 \uc0\u8594 
\f1\b0 \cf2  PD/LGD/EAD findings
\f3\b \cf2 \uc0\u8594 
\f1\b0 \cf2  capital/pricing worked example
\f3\b \cf2 \uc0\u8594 
\f1\b0 \cf2    limitations.\
\'95 Capital/pricing implications: one worked EL example, tied to how a lender would actually use it (loan-loss reserve sizing, risk-based pricing spread) \'97 interpretation only, not a full capital-modeling exercise.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs44 \cf2 6. Future / open items \'97 not part of this pass\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs40 \cf2 \'95 Hosmer-Lemeshow goodness-of-fit test \'97 deferred to the end of the project.\
\'95 LGD / EAD backtesting on the FY2000\'962009 recession window \'97 PD-side backtesting and PSI are already done (see Section 4); LGD/EAD backtesting on the same population is deferred until the whitepaper is largely written.\
\'95 ECB SAFE survey cross-market comparison \'97 future goal, not active work.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs44 \cf2 7. Reference note\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs40 \cf2 Moody's SME ABS rating methodology was used only as an external reality-check source for PD/EL benchmark numbers already incorporated into this project \'97 not as the basis for a full comparative-methodology write-up.\
\
\'97\'97\'97\
